Here's a suggestion (or maybe a plug for some information if it already 
exists..) ....

Since it's possible to teleport between levels, why must going to the lowest
levels result in one being sent to Hell?  I mean, if you really teleport 
down far enough, you will start to ascend to the other side of the world, 
like China.   :-)

Things could be very strange on the other side of the world -- a wierd 
flip-side to Hack?  I'm not sure what useful purpose this might serve, 
except to bring in new (and controversial) tools and weapons that didn't 
exist in older versions of (non-net) Hack.  Instead of completely new 
monsters etc, they could be remapped or pointed to each other, so you
wouldn't know what a Gnome is anymore -- on the flip side.  Thus, the 
only lure would be the treasures you might find!

For all I know, teleporting past Hell may already exist in NetHack 3.0 -- 
I've become pretty good at 1.0.3 beta (!) Hack, and have only recently 
got NetHack (I've been asleep for years, really..).  SO, this is a whole 
new world to me!  (and no, I would prefer not to have a spoiler file!!)
